.TH auto-change-nfsd-count 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-change-nfsd-count - Change the number of nfsd(8) processes/threads

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-change-nfsd-count minimum maximum
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
minimum     The minimum number of NFS server processes to keep running
maximum     The maximum number of NFS server processes to run
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-change-nfsd-count
command sets the minimum and maximum number of nfsd(1) processes
or threads.  Some systems, such as FreeBSD, use threads and
dynamically adjust the number of threads to meet load.
Others, such as RHEL, use a fixed number of heavyweight processes,
in which case the "minimum" argument is ignored, and the number
of processes will be the "maximum" argument.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-change-nfsd-count
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/exports
.ad
.fi

